// PAS-DEBT-B2-010b Slice B (#1541, v0.36.65) — round-trip fixture.
//
// Two-fragment macro exercising the parser's structured template
// output on a template that repeats each fragment reference twice.
// Under Slice B, `swap(p, q)` composes into the source
// `{ let t = p; p = q; q = t; }` (both `$a` sites resolve to `p`,
// both `$b` sites to `q`), demonstrating that duplicate fragment
// references in the template all bind consistently to the same
// pattern-side capture.
//
// End-to-end code-emission coverage waits on the macro-driver work
// (PAS-DEBT-B7-001, #1529).

module M = structure {
  macro swap($a:expr, $b:expr) => { { let t = $a; $a = $b; $b = t; } }
}
